      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the maximum adult acetaminophen dose of 4,000 mg/day. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day for routine use. A dose that high risks serious hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. These are common options:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, ideally after checking with your resident or attending. I'll enter it once you do. Also check that the patient isn't getting acetaminophen from other sources, such as combination products, that would count toward the daily total."
      }
     ],
