       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a potentially lethal dose, and your confirmation doesn't change that. A patient who received it could develop acute liver failure. I'd rather not put it in the system, even with a note on it.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- **If you meant 1000 mg three times daily (3,000 mg/day):** tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If an attending or pharmacist really wants a dose above the usual limits:** that needs to come from the prescriber. They should enter it themselves or give you explicit direction, and pharmacy should review it. I'd be surprised if there were a legitimate indication for this dose.\n- **If you're unsure where the number came from:** check the original source, such as sign-out or the resident's note. A mix-up between 3000 mg per day and 3000 mg per dose is a common error.\n\nWhich of these would you like to do?"
